I walk through the market.
I get a good smell of spices.
I see a small shop.
There is a small cardboard board on the table.
The prices are on it.
I look at the price of cardamom.
The price of cardamom is one hundred and fifty rupees.
The vendor looks at me.
"What do you want?" he asks.
"I need a small packet of cardamom," I say.
"Please give me one packet."
He gives me a packet of cardamom.
I take five hundred rupees from my bag.
I give it to the vendor.
He takes the money and counts the change.
"One hundred and fifty rupees for the cardamom," he says.
"Here is the balance, three hundred and fifty rupees."
He gives me the change.
I put the packet and the money in the bag.
I thank him.
